# A real RAR archive of two generated fixture pages, base64-encoded.
#
# RAR compression is proprietary and there is no free writer, so no CI
# runner can build one — which left the reader untested everywhere but a
# developer machine with WinRAR. These are the genuine bytes of an archive
# written once by `Rar.exe`, carried as text so the repository stays free of
# committed binaries. The pages inside are this project's own fixtures.
#
